      "narrative": "The question hangs in the air. Mara Venn's brow furrows \u2014 not in anger, but in confusion. She tilts her head, studying you like you've just said something odd.\n\n\"Filed?\" She repeats the word slowly, tasting it. \"The lock wasn't *filed,* Kael. It was sealed. Toran forged it, set the wards, and the Guild locked it. There's no record of anyone filing or altering it after that.\" She sets her cup down with a soft clack. \"Unless you mean something else. What exactly are you asking?\"\n\nThere's a flicker in her eyes \u2014 not recognition, but curiosity. She's trying to follow your thread, but you've lost her. Your question was imprecise, the wrong word catching on her ear like a burr on wool.\n\nBehind her, at the bar, **Toran Vex** glances up from his rag. He heard his name. His fingers tighten on the cloth, and he watches the two of you with the nervous alertness of a man who expects bad news.\n\nMara waits for you to clarify. Her sharp eyes haven't left your face.\n\nWhat do you say to her?"
    },
