      "narrative": "Mara's lips press into a thin line. She holds your gaze for a moment, then exhales through her nose and leans back in her chair.\n\n\"I already told you. The Guild ran the passage. They kept the lock, the whole operation \u2014 but the man who worked the ferry was Old Bram. He's the one who took the coin and pulled the rope.\" She gestures vaguely toward the shuttered window, toward the unseen gate beyond. \"That's what I know. If there was someone else \u2014 some middleman, some broker \u2014 I never heard of them.\"\n\nBut there's a tightness in her jaw now. You pushed, and she gave the same answer, and the repeated question has frayed something. She doesn't look suspicious of *you* \u2014 she looks like a woman who has told you everything she knows and is growing tired of being asked the same thing.\n\nAt the bar, **Toran Vex** has stopped pretending to wipe the counter. He's just standing there, rag in hand, watching the two of you with wide, unblinking eyes.\n\nMara picks up her cup, drains it, and sets it down with a hollow thunk. \"Is there something specific you're looking for, Kael? Because if you've got a question you're not asking, you might as well ask it.\""
    },
