      "narrative": "The walk back passes in silence. The lane narrows between the leaning buildings, and the morning light struggles to reach the mud below. A shutter creaks somewhere overhead. The dog is still nosing through the refuse, having dragged a scrap of leather into the open.\n\nThe Copper Finch's door groans as you push it open. Inside, the tavern is dim after the grey daylight \u2014 the lamps still burning low, the air thick with the smell of old smoke and spilled ale. A few patrons occupy scattered tables, none of them looking up.\n\nYour old table \u2014 the one near the wall, scarred with initials and ring-stains \u2014 is empty. As you sit, the wood creaks beneath your weight.\n\n**Mara Venn** is still there, at the same table she was at before. She glances up as you enter, then returns to studying a folded piece of parchment spread before her. **Toran Vex** is behind the bar, wiping the same cup with the same rag, his eyes fixed on the door you just walked through. He looks away the moment you catch him watching.\n\nThe tavern settles back into its low hum. A log shifts in the hearth. Nothing seems to have changed in your absence \u2014 but the air feels heavier now, charged with unasked questions.\n\nWhat do you do?"
